Z||000008||theogre||01-29-2000||12:03 PM||||I had forgotten about the ECM temp lockout. That on it's own would account for it. If you have or can borrow an ECM scanner you can actually watch the ECM lockup signal.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||01-29-2000||02:30 PM||||Where would I find one?  Are they fairly simple to use?  What are we talking about replacing anyway?  The ECM?  I don't think I want to spend the $$ for one of those.  The car doesn't run well, but it does run.  Start me towards the next step.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||01-29-2000||08:27 PM||||The ECM scanner I use is AutoXrays GM only scanner. (Simmilar to their XP240 but only for GM cars and much cheaper.) This scanner comes with the cable to hook it up and is 150-180$us. It will work with nearly all GM cars from 81-95. <P>The thing comes in handy when you want to test a sensor. It will report every sensor the ECM uses. It will also report cruise control on the ECMs that do that. (cruise is not part of the ECM on all models before around 89.)<P>In your TC lockup case, I don't think it's really much wrong to worry about. If that's all that's up.<P>If your just jumping in and going then 3 miles is a pretty reasonable warm up time. Now if you have other problems that are sensor related then a scanner is handy. <P>Thing one is stuff in a new 195 stant thermostat. If the T'stat isn't closing all the way it will slow warmup. <P>I like the 180 thermostat, but in cold weather the engine never seems to really want to get warm. (I did end up stuffing a new 195 in mine for this east coast winter. It warms up sooner, and runs close to the same temp. I'll stuff the 180 back in in spring to keep the performance.)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||01-30-2000||06:12 AM||||ogre--Thanx, but I guess I'd have to pass on the scanner.  I probably have sensors that are bad, but for that kind of $$ I'll have to figure something else out.  If I ever decide that I need one in the future, where can I get one?  Autozone?  I will get a 195 thermostat, though.  I guess it couldn't hurt and they can't be that expensive.  <P>I need to at least check everything with my code key, but in my quest for a better (custom made) ECM cover/center console, I've buried my ADLSLC thing somewhere underneath.  Maybe one of these days when it warms up I'll get to it. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||01-31-2000||04:14 AM||||My tcc doesn't lock up until my car warms up a little... so yeah it's temp related.. just had to get my view in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ogre - Wasn't the cruise on 87-88 4cyl Fiero's controlled by the ecm?  I could swear I saw that somewhere..||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||01-31-2000||06:38 PM||||87-88 4 cyl only. I don't think the V6 ECM took that function untill the 89-91 range.||||reg||1
